When the reconfiguration with sync is for the MCG, according to [1] Clause 5.3.5.5.2, the UE:

* applies the value of the newUE-Identity as the C-RNTI.

The UE also handles the lower layers for the target SpCell by:

* stopping timer T310 for the corresponding SpCell, if running;
* stopping timer T312 for the corresponding SpCell, if running;
* resuming MCG transmission, if suspended.

Additionally, for the target L2 U2N Relay UE, the UE:
* considers the target L2 U2N Relay UE to be the one indicated by the targetRelayUEIdentity in the sl-PathSwitchConfig;
* starts timer T420 for the corresponding target L2 U2N Relay UE with the timer value set to T420, as included in the sl-PathSwitchConfig;
* performs the PC5-RRC connection establishment with the target L2 U2N Relay UE indicated by the targetRelayUEIdentity, if needed. 

